# Scoped Trivy allowlist — review and prune when upstream ships a fix.
#
# supercronic v0.2.49 (latest, published 2026-08-14) ships a binary built with
# Go stdlib 1.26.6, which carries these two FIXABLE HIGH CVEs:
#   CVE-2026-78667  net/http  DoS via crafted HTTP Range headers  (fixed in Go 1.26.9/1.27.2)
#   CVE-2026-97031  crypto/tls DoS via multiple ECH outer extension refs (fixed in Go 1.26.9/1.27.2)
# Both are denial-of-service, not RCE. In this image supercronic only runs the
# local cron that execs the Python sync — no HTTP listener (no
# -prometheus-listen-address) and no TLS client — so neither code path is
# reachable. Upstream has no rebuilt release yet (v0.2.49 is latest).
#
# Remove both lines once supercronic publishes a release built with Go >= 1.26.9.
# Re-review by: 2026-11-15
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031
